ented data. Keep early stopping (patience=5) and save best model. Preserve variable names (train_loader, val_loader, model, optimizer, scheduler) and existing evaluate_deberta and compute_log_loss functions."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
  "reason": "Execution results confirm severe overfitting of DeBERTa (val loss spikes from 0.3057 epoch 4 to 0.4914 epoch 5, and final DeBERTa weight in ensemble is only 0.1, indicating poor generalization). The initial plan proposes freeze-thaw fine-tuning, attention pooling, and focal loss. Similar successful historical experiments show that freeze-thaw and focal loss stabilize training and improve DeBERTa contributions. Therefore, I focus on model_design to implement attention pooling and focal loss, and training_evaluation to implement freeze-thaw and stylistic augmentation. Data processing is already comprehensive and does not need changes.",
